note Translated from Go sort.Search (go/src/sort/search.go, lines 58 to 73).

to search n f
    given n is an Int
    note GAP: a parameter whose type is an operation - Go passes f as func(int) bool; the doc has no type for an operation value, so "an Operation from Int to Bool" is a guess
    given f is an Operation from Int to Bool
    produces an Int
    note UNCLEAR: Go lets f do anything (read state, do I/O). The doc has no way to say "uses whatever f uses", so this header is pure only if every f passed in is pure

    note Define f(-1) is false and f(n) is true.
    var i starts at 0
    var j starts at n
    repeat while i is less than j
        invariant i is 0 or not f (i - 1)
        invariant j is n or f j
        decreases j - i
        note WORKAROUND: Go writes int(uint(i+j) >> 1) to avoid overflow; the doc has no unsigned reinterpretation and no shift, so the overflow-free form from example 10 is used
        let h be i + (j - i) / 2
        note i is at most h, and h is less than j
        if not f h
            note preserves f(i - 1) is false
            set i to h + 1
        otherwise
            note preserves f(j) is true
            set j to h
    note i is j, f(i - 1) is false, and f(j) is true, so the answer is i
    give back i
